"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[7267],{47267:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"yandex-data-centry-ataki-sboi-oblako","locale":"en","title":"Attacks on 3 Yandex data centers over 4 days disrupt dozens of services","description":"From October 8 to 11, 2026, attacks hit 3 Yandex data centers with up to 115 MW of combined capacity. Which services failed and why recovery will be expensive.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"On October 8, 2026, a drone attack and fire halted Yandex\'s data center in Sasovo, Ryazan Region, with about 12 MW of capacity. On October 9, its Kaluga center, rated at 63 MW with more than 3800 server racks, was damaged. On October 11, the Vladimir center, about 40 MW, stopped completely. Together, these sites represent up to 115 MW, about 6% of Russia\'s total data-center capacity of roughly 1.8 GW. Nobody was injured in the Vladimir attack. Yandex has not disclosed the damage or equipment-repair timeline."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Disruptions affected Yandex Go, Pay, Mail, Maps and Eats. Taxi bookings also failed in Kazakhstan, Belarus, Armenia and Serbia. Third-party services renting Yandex Cloud capacity went down too, including Cian, several developers\' websites and Astral\'s electronic document-exchange system. On October 11, Yandex said services were gradually returning, but fintech head Dmitry Pirogov said on October 12 that a full Yandex Pay recovery timeline could not yet be given."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Cloud computing means renting another company\'s servers. A business pays for capacity instead of building its own data center, which is convenient while the site works. It resembles a family keeping all its money on one card at one bank: if the card is blocked, it cannot pay. The defense is a copy at another site, known as redundancy. That means paying for 2 sets of capacity instead of 1, so many businesses economize on it. Yandex Cloud is divided into zones at separate data centers, but 2 of its 4 zones failed, in Vladimir and Sasovo. The company called the remaining zones unstable, advised clients to prepare backup sites, and agreed with VK Cloud, Selectel and K2Cloud that they would quickly host clients\' data and services."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"Recovery will be expensive. Servers and neural-network accelerators are scarce worldwide because of AI demand. Market participants estimate delivery times from 2–3 to 6 months. Mobile Research Group\'s Eldar Murtazin says equipment in Russia became 10–15% more expensive within days. RUVDS\'s Nikita Tsaplin says some data centers are already strengthening equipment protection, with costs likely to enter client prices. Strategy Partners\' Sergei Kudryashov estimates Yandex Cloud revenue at about 30 billion rubles, 2–4% of group revenue. Cloud is a small business for Yandex itself, but its main services run on the same data centers."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"For an ordinary user, the outage meant unavailable taxis or payments. The indirect route is longer. If cloud services become more expensive because of equipment and protection costs, businesses renting them will pass some expenses into their own service prices. Nobody has yet estimated how much."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"Businesses face an unpleasant choice. A second site or a move to another provider costs money now while equipment is scarce. Staying with one provider is cheaper, but the next outage would stop sales again. When Yandex will restore its previous capacity remains unknown."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"Which Yandex data centers were attacked in October 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"The Sasovo site in Ryazan Region, about 12 MW, stopped on October 8. The 63 MW Kaluga data center was damaged on October 9. The Vladimir data center, about 40 MW, stopped on October 11."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Which services failed because of the Yandex data-center attacks?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"Disruptions affected Yandex Go, Yandex Pay, Mail, Maps, Eats and cloud clients such as Cian and Astral. Taxi bookings also failed in Kazakhstan, Belarus, Armenia and Serbia."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"When will Yandex services recover?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"The company gives no precise timeline. Services are gradually returning, but replacement equipment takes 2 to 6 months to arrive. On October 12, Yandex Pay said it could not yet state a recovery timeline."}],"sources":[{"label":"Yandex data-center attack triggers cascading outages: who was affected?","url":"https://thebell.io/ataka-na-data-tsentr-yandeksa-vyzvala-tsepnuyu-reaktsiyu-sboev-kto-postradal"},{"label":"Drone attacks on Yandex data centers cause outages and threaten higher cloud prices","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9024163"},{"label":"Drones attack a third Yandex data center in a week","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/10/11/droni-atakovali-tretii-data-tsentr-yandeksa-zanedelyu-a208309"},{"label":"Drone attack on Yandex\'s Vladimir data center: incident details","url":"https://www.fontanka.ru/2026/10/11/76693363/"},{"label":"Consequences of attacks on Yandex data centers: expert views","url":"https://www.fontanka.ru/2026/10/11/76693413/"},{"label":"Another Yandex outage: Vladimir data center halted and ru-central1-a zone unavailable","url":"https://www.comss.ru/page.php?id=22366"},{"label":"Yandex Pay unable to give a service-recovery timeline","url":"https://vz.ru/news/2026/10/12/1461835.html"}],"sourceBodySha256":"90f104461afebdbd416e2a7cbc14c93eb9a1629170e459918558786e22c1b0b1"}')}}]);